// automations.memql -- safety namespace.

// purgeExpiredSafetyClassifications
// =================================
//
// Daily 02:35 UTC sweep over v1:safety:classification rows older
// than MEMQL_SAFETY_CLASSIFICATION_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90).
// Mirrors purgeExpiredPolicyTraces in platform/: MemQL has no
// row-removal mutation today, so this cron emits a
// `safety.classification.retention.observed` event each tick with
// the candidate count. Flip to per-row delete once the engine
// grows a delete() mutation.
//
// Schedule chosen as 02:35 UTC (5 minutes after policyTrace's
// 02:30 sweep) so the two retention crons don't contend on the
// same DB window.
/// Daily 02:35 UTC sweep: identifies safety-classification rows past
/// MEMQL_SAFETY_CLASSIFICATION_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90). Observation-only until MemQL gains
/// row-removal support.
automation purgeExpiredSafetyClassifications @trigger(schedule="0 35 2 * * *") => logic purgeExpiredSafetyClassifications

// purgeExpiredOutputScreenings (memql#233)
// =======================================
//
// Daily 02:40 UTC sweep over v1:safety:outputScreening rows older
// than MEMQL_SAFETY_OUTPUT_SCREENING_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90).
// Same observation-only pattern as purgeExpiredSafetyClassifications.
// Offset by 5 minutes so the two safety crons don't contend.
/// Daily 02:40 UTC sweep: identifies output-screening rows past
/// MEMQL_SAFETY_OUTPUT_SCREENING_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90). Observation-only until MemQL gains
/// row-removal support.
automation purgeExpiredOutputScreenings @trigger(schedule="0 40 2 * * *") => logic purgeExpiredOutputScreenings
